Etymon comes from Greek etymos: true, real, actual—hence etymology as study of a word’s historical/original sense. 

But entomology comes from Greek entomon, from entomos: cut into pieces / segmented, referring to insects’ divided bodies. Our word insect is essentially the Latin version of the same “cut into” idea. 

